[h1]Worker Optimizer[/h1]
[b]Auto-assign workers to suitable jobs with one click.[/b]

Match your residents' specialties to your settlement's needs, cover minimum operating crews first and keep the saved reserve free for construction.

[h2]v0.3.0-preview[/h2]
[b]In-game validation is pending.[/b] Includes corrected job eligibility, worker-change ordering and recovery without permanently locking the icon. Test on a separate save first.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One manual icon:[/b] always visible; click to request assignment. No settings gear, logbook view or visibility shortcut.
[*][b]Smart assignment:[/b] considers worker specialties, productivity and job requirements.
[*][b]Coverage first:[/b] select feasible minimum crews before filling extra workplaces by suitability.
[*][b]Equal priority:[/b] all active supported buildings use the same priority; older priority overrides and strict/weighted mode choices are ignored.
[*][b]Saved builder reserve:[/b] respect the previously saved number of eligible residents to keep free, or 1 by default. This preview has no reserve editor.
[*][b]Manual only:[/b] automatic schedules are disabled, including those saved by earlier releases.
[*][b]Targeted moves:[/b] safely account for the optional workers affected by replacing a required worker.
[/list]

Earlier settings and history are retained, but cannot be edited in this preview.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[b]Recommended timing:[/b] For the first test, run assignment at night or just after a new day starts. Daytime behavior still needs separate validation.

Subscribe and restart after Steam downloads the update. Use either Workshop or a local installation, never both.

Click the lower-left assignment icon. Check results in the game's building and resident windows.

The icon stays busy until the run ends. Extra clicks do not cancel or restart it. Only observed changes count; confirmed changes are not automatically rolled back.

[b]Please note:[/b] paused and unsupported buildings retain their workers. The builder reserve and job requirements remain binding, so shortages can still leave buildings unstaffed. Keep a backup save.

